# P, THE OPERATION INDEX, AS A RELATION OF ITS OWN. One row per operation a filing declares.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE OTHER CONFORMED DIMENSION, AND IT WAS THE ONLY ONE WITHOUT A FILE. `draw` and
#    `induction` are both P x L fact tables, `layer` has layers/every_layer.sqlc, and `operation`
#    had nothing. So every question about operations reached through an ENTRY table and got the
#    operations that happen to have entries, rather than the operations that exist. The two
#    coincide today only because `pm:Operation` requires at least one draw or induction, which is
#    a fact about the grammar that no query stated.
#
# ⛔ A DIMENSION WITHOUT A FILE CANNOT BE A LEFT OPERAND, so no law in algebra/ could ever have
#   governed a count of operations, and diagrams/roster.sqlc's `tasks` law would have had nothing
#   to count against. Same repair as composition/carriable.sqlc and
#   composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc: the difference needs a named left operand.
-- pm:Operation, keyed (filing, label).
SELECT o.filing, o.label
FROM pm.operation o
